---
description: Rules for modifying and creating new pages in the Next.js app
globs: next-app/app/**/page.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---
[nextjs.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nextjs.mdc)

- All pages live in `next-app/app/` directory following App Router conventions
- Pages are Server Components by default (no `'use client'` directive needed)
- Use async Server Components for data fetching
- Check authentication using `getAuthenticatedUser()` from `@/lib/pocketbase-server`
- Redirect unauthorized users using `redirect()` from `next/navigation`
- Import layout metadata from `next/metadata` if needed
- Use nested folders for routes (e.g., `app/dashboard/page.tsx` for `/dashboard`)
- Use dynamic segments with brackets (e.g., `app/profile/[id]/page.tsx` for `/profile/123`)
- Group related routes with route groups using parentheses (e.g., `app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`)
